Body:
@blakkd I checked the current implementation and reads still warm the LSP via `lsp.touchFile(filepath)` in `src/tool/read.ts`, while write/edit/apply_patch call `touchFile(..., "document")` and wait for diagnostics.

So I don’t think changing this to “as files are written” is quite accurate. The sidebar copy is maybe broader than ideal, though, because activation can happen on reads and writes. Maybe a better message would be:

> LSPs will activate as files are accessed
